  "notes": "Lifted most of this from Lilburgh and Darryl Wyke on Brewer's Friend. Lots of overlap between them.\nhttps://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/recipe/view/210070/blood-orange-ipa-clone\nhttps://www.brewersfriend.com/homebrew/recipe/view/1047763/blood-orange\n\nFor the adventurous, we have the option to add in some pureed orange around 1.015 to add an extra fruity kick. Current plan is to rack off into two smaller secondary fermenters around then to compare and contrast fruit-full and fruit-less! If we want to bottle any of this we will want to take a crack at pasteurizing any of the fruited version to keep them from literally exploding.",
